{{!--
List items (<li>) linking to the social accounts of the author in the current context.
Use it inside an author context (the author block of author.hbs, primary_author, foreach authors)
and wrap it in a <ul> guarded by {{#has any="website, twitter, facebook, linkedin, bluesky, threads, mastodon, tiktok, youtube, instagram"}}.

Each link is guarded by {{#if <platform>}} on purpose: {{social_url}} looks the platform up
on the current author first and then falls back to the site's own account (@site), so an
unguarded call would show the site's account on every author.
The X account is still stored in the "twitter" field (social_url type="twitter" outputs an x.com URL).
Platforms with a glyph in the icon font use it; the others use an inline SVG from partials/icons/.
--}}
{{#if website}}
  <li>
    <a href="{{website}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{t "Website"}}">
      <span class="icon-globe" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
  </li>
{{/if}}
{{#if twitter}}
  <li>
    <a href="{{social_url type="twitter"}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="X">
      {{> "icons/x"}}
    </a>
  </li>
{{/if}}
{{#if facebook}}
  <li>
    <a href="{{social_url type="facebook"}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Facebook">
      <span class="icon-facebook" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
  </li>
{{/if}}
